          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">What Is Pyorrhea (Gum Disease)?</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
            Pyorrhea (periodontitis) is a common gum infection that starts gently as swollen or bleeding gums (gingivitis) when plaque and tartar stay trapped along the gum edge. Over time, bacteria move deeper beneath the gums, creating pockets around the tooth roots and slowly weakening the bone that keeps teeth firm. Treating gum disease early helps keep gums pink, comfortable, and supportive.
          </p>
